{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "021L", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$T$", "MATH_0002": "$\\{T_i \\to T\\}_{i \\in I}$", "MATH_0003": "$T$", "MATH_0004": "$\\{U_j \\to T\\}_{j = 1, \\ldots, m}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\{T_i \\to T\\}_{i \\in I}$", "MATH_0006": "$U_j$", "MATH_0007": "$U_j$", "MATH_0008": "$T_i$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-fppf-affine}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:70f5bcb2ae6ec87aa1fc2d0b5609686c27090116cc9aa3e1bd5d33260e5c7028", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:1de3b5b0063881effaa2dcbdffd98d7e11e9642d7241f67ad9776b4bf9ce4ccc", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be an affine scheme.\nLet <MATH_0002> be an fppf covering of <MATH_0003>.\nThen there exists an fppf covering\n<MATH_0004> which is a refinement\nof <MATH_0005> such that each <MATH_0006> is an affine\nscheme. Moreover, we may choose each <MATH_0007> to be open affine\nin one of the <MATH_0008>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:0f4ab24eb950bff0419631dd77316c4dcf3434e8d75e31b9b3846f8e3076b192", "unit_id": "tag:021P:statement"}
{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "021L", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{morphisms-lemma-fppf-open}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d3cd8dd651d5650544b3b6278429ae5244b2794b997ab37cac8e6629aa2fdc3e", "source_text": "This follows directly from the definitions using that a\nmorphism which is flat and locally of finite presentation is open,\nsee Morphisms, Lemma <REF_0001>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:c64df30813bd48f64adbe4ed1d93e842f7f7588dd4642b3d6df6e5756f27721e", "unit_id": "tag:021P:proof"}
{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "021L", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:6945887321fe30912185bfe21c93363c5ca2e2a223ff071a1d0afa8ad2cf0e45", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThus we define the corresponding standard coverings of affines as follows.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:c6fc6acd5442ae08d942785456938b46f7474665c094eb74d77f623a49f76092", "unit_id": "tag:021L:prose-0003"}
{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "021L", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$T$", "MATH_0002": "$T$", "MATH_0003": "$\\{f_j : U_j \\to T\\}_{j = 1, \\ldots, m}$", "MATH_0004": "$U_j$", "MATH_0005": "$T$", "MATH_0006": "$T = \\bigcup f_j(U_j)$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-standard-fppf}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:7d2706466bb0058bd4dd583aed6befd574271a106036ff6e165ae642030d1604", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:fbd2ba398e682605fe54ecb88c845a84bbcbab9331e04e2f2ab80bb9932bd0b9", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be an affine scheme. A <TEXTITOPEN_0001>standard fppf covering<TEXTITCLOSE_0001>\nof <MATH_0002> is a family <MATH_0003>\nwith each <MATH_0004> is affine, flat and of finite presentation over <MATH_0005>\nand <MATH_0006>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:e101f56eaa2a4e323f65ba333c6a372c46abecc95865268500c51de48ee95246", "unit_id": "tag:021Q:statement"}
{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "021L", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\Sch_{fppf}$", "MATH_0002": "$S_0$", "MATH_0003": "$\\text{Cov}_0$", "MATH_0004": "$\\Sch_\\alpha$", "MATH_0005": "$S_0$", "MATH_0006": "$\\Sch_\\alpha$", "MATH_0007": "$\\text{Cov}_0$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{sites-definition-site}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{sets-lemma-construct-category}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{sets-lemma-coverings-site}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\end{enumerate}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-big-fppf-site}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:7f9f7a1ee999e32633b0ec14a2cd14a015c4b805180fd4565d739a5e54773c11", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b455072deba30e40ea1f766a9d4c8d55fe4688c01aa7468a6c4bba86cc23708a", "source_text": "A <TEXTITOPEN_0001>big fppf site<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> is any site <MATH_0001> as in\nSites, Definition <REF_0001> constructed as follows:\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> Choose any set of schemes <MATH_0002>, and any set of fppf coverings\n<MATH_0003> among these schemes.\n<STRUCT_0003> As underlying category take any category <MATH_0004>\nconstructed as in Sets, Lemma <REF_0002>\nstarting with the set <MATH_0005>.\n<STRUCT_0004> Choose any set of coverings as in\nSets, Lemma <REF_0003> starting with the\ncategory <MATH_0006> and the class of fppf coverings,\nand the set <MATH_0007> chosen above.\n<STRUCT_0005>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:9c07bcd97d54cfacbe035064a899d719715233e64a5869f0cb34a9db08fcb7b1", "unit_id": "tag:021R:statement"}
